WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
A car pulls away from one
junction and stops at the next,

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.260
thirty seconds later.

3
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.380
All the way, its speedometer
needle rises, then falls.

4
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.180
It tells you speed, never distance.

5
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:17.700
Its speed is modelled by v equals three
t minus nought point one t squared,

6
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.310
in metres per second.

7
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.970
So how far apart are the junctions?

8
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.070
Top speed times the time?

9
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.780
In this mission, you'll learn integration:

10
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.200
differentiation run in reverse.

11
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:33.350
You'll meet the constant of integration,
and use one known point to pin down a

12
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.970
whole curve.

13
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.180
Then you'll evaluate definite
integrals, with a limit at each end.

14
00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.450
Your mission: work out
how far the car goes.
